## Refactor Status Section

At the end of each code move, update the related document with:

```md
## Refactor Status

Status: planned | in-progress | moved | split | replaced | deleted
Old path:
New path:
Related files:
Imports updated:
Typecheck status:
Notes:
```

## Dismounting Rule

When extracting a component out of a file that currently contains multiple components:

1. Create the new component file.
2. Create a matching markdown document in:

```txt
.docs/developer/refactors/components
```

3. Link it back to the original component document.
4. Update the original component document with:

```md
## Dismounted Components

| Component | New code path | New documentation path | Reason |
|---|---|---|
```

## Phase Completion Rule

No refactor phase is complete unless:

- code state and documentation state agree
- old and new paths are recorded
- moved/split files have matching docs
- unresolved risks are written down
- typecheck/lint status is recorded when available

Documentation and code move together. Otherwise the next agent run inherits a crime scene.
